!**/.env.example
# Per-app production env. Ploy dropped the `env:` block from ploy.yaml (env
# vars now come from Ploy project settings + a local .env), so the public
# build-time NEXT_PUBLIC_* literals that used to live there are committed here
# instead — that keeps the prod build reproducible from the repo. These hold
# ONLY public values (cross-app URLs, public embed key, write-only PostHog
# key). Public by design — never put secrets here; a real env var set in Ploy
# project settings overrides these at build time.
!apps/showcase/.env.production
!apps/admin/.env.production
!apps/dashboard/.env.production
!apps/docs/.env.production
!apps/marketing/.env.production
